    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49364" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tŭder</span></b> , ĕris,
			n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Umbria</i>, <i>near the Tiber</i>, now
				<i>Todi</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 14,
				19, § 113</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 6,
			645</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tŭders</span></b> ,
			ertis, <i>adj. m.</i>, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Tuder; as subst.</i>,
				<i>an inhabitant of Tuder</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 4,
			222</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 464</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 1228</span></i> and
			3726.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tŭder-nis</span></b> ,
			is, <i>adj. f.</i>, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Tuder</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 3, 4, § 36</span></i>
			.</div>
